From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] perf(LibraryBanner): clip the collage with a scissor, not a canvas group

The home banner's collage of twelve tilted library tiles sits in a
TextureRect with clip_children = CLIP_CHILDREN_AND_DRAW. That makes the
renderer draw the tiles into an offscreen canvas group every frame and
composite them back through the TextureRect's texture as a mask -- and
that texture is a GradientTexture2D whose two stops are both opaque
black, so the mask is the whole rectangle. All it does is clip the
tilted tiles to the banner's bounds.

clip_contents does exactly that with a scissor rectangle, with no
offscreen pass. The TextureRect still draws its black texture under the
tiles, so the banner looks the same.

Measured on a MANGMI Air X (Adreno 610, 1920x1080, OGUI redrawing
continuously), Godot's own viewport GPU timer: 19.6 -> 13.9 ms per
frame. The card and icon clip masks are real shape masks (rounded
corners, icon shapes) and are left alone.

(qforge: ours, for upstream.)
---
--- a/core/ui/components/library_banner.tscn
+++ b/core/ui/components/library_banner.tscn
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 script = ExtResource("1_yhxxp")
 
 [node name="TextureRect" type="TextureRect" parent="."]
-clip_children = 2
+clip_contents = true
 layout_mode = 1
 anchors_preset = 15
 anchor_right = 1.0
